<title>UKRAINE: Ukraine cuts '97 sugar beet crop forecast.</title>
<headline>Ukraine cuts '97 sugar beet crop forecast.</headline>
<dateline>KIEV 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ukraine has revised down its forecast for the 1997 sugar beet crop to 27 million tonnes from 30-31 million tonnes, Interfax news agency quoted an agriculture official as saying on Friday.</p>
<p>It gave no reason for the revised forecast, which it attributed to Deputy Prime Minister in charge of agriculture Mikhailo Zubets.  </p>
<p>Last year's crop was 24 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Ukraine, a major exporter of white sugar to Russia, had previously forecast flat refined sugar output of 3.26 million tonnes this year.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
